B.axz=new A.G(B.aDt,['title: child_start\n---\n<<if has("ch2_done")>>\n    <<if has("brave")>>\n        Tali: I told Mum I am not scared of orcs. I lied. But I told her.\n        You: That counts. That is most of what brave is.\n    <<else>>\n        Tali: I made a map of every hiding place in the village. For when it matters.\n        You: Smartest thing anyone has done here all year.\n    <<endif>>\n<<elseif has("ch2_open")>>\n    <<jump child_ch2_back>>\n<<elseif has("ch1_done") and level() >= 12>>\n    <<jump child_ch2>>\n<<elseif has("ch1_done")>>\n    Tali: I practise every day! Come back when you are stronger, and show me.\n<<elseif has("ch1_open")>>\n    <<jump child_ch1_back>>\n<<else>>\n    <<jump child_ch1>>\n<<endif>>\n===\ntitle: child_ch1\n---\nTali: Are you a warrior? Mum says orcs eat children.\nYou: I woke up on a beach last week. I am still working out what I am.\nTali: Then you can help me. Nobody can know. Swear it.\nTali: I went to the meadow to fight a slime. Alone. With my sword.\nTali: It went badly. The slime kept the sword.\n-> "You could have been hurt."\n    Tali: That is what Mum would say. Do not be a Mum.\n    <<rep child 2>>\n-> "Then you lost a sword, and I am not your mother."\n    You: You lost a sword. That is the whole story. Go home and stay there.\n    Tali: ...I thought you were a warrior.\n    <<rep child -12>>\n-> "How big was this slime?"\n    Tali: Huge! As big as... a big dog. A wet one.\n    <<rep child 5>>\nTali: It is by the old stones in the meadow. Please. Before she counts the wood.\n<<flag ch1_open>>\n===\ntitle: child_ch1_back\n---\n<<if has_item("q_tali_sword")>>\n    Tali: You found it! Is it hurt? Oh, it is sticky.\n    You: Slimes will do that. Hold it like this, thumb on top.\n    Tali: Did you fight the slime for it? Was it the big one?\n    -> Tell her it was the biggest slime you ever saw.\n        You: Biggest one I have ever seen. You were lucky to get away.\n        Tali: I KNEW it.\n        <<rep child 10>>\n    -> Tell her it was small, and the size is not the point.\n        You: It was small. And it still nearly had you. Remember that.\n        Tali: ...Oh. Okay. I will remember.\n        <<rep child 10>>\n        <<flag honest>>\n    <<take q_tali_sword>>\n    <<flag ch1_done>>\n    <<reward child_1>>\n<<else>>\n    Tali: The old stones, in the meadow! Have you got it yet? Be quiet about it!\n<<endif>>\n===\ntitle: child_ch2\n---\nTali: Teach me about the East Gate. Everyone stops talking when I walk in.\nTali: Mum says orcs eat children. Uncle says that is silly. They both look scared.\nYou: You want to know what is really out there.\nTali: Guard Brek knows. He will not tell me. He tells grown-ups, and you count.\n<<flag ch2_open>>\n===\ntitle: child_ch2_back\n---\n<<if has("asked_brek")>>\n    Tali: Well? What did Brek say? Do they really eat children?\n    -> "No. But they are real, and they are close."\n        You: Nobody has seen them eat anyone. But they are real, and they are close.\n        Tali: So that is why everyone is whispering.\n        Tali: I think I would rather know. I am going to be brave about it.\n        <<flag brave>>\n        <<rep child 25>>\n    -> "Stay near the huts, and learn where to hide."\n        You: Brave people are not the ones who run at things. Learn the hiding places.\n        Tali: That is what you would say if it was bad.\n        You: It is what I would say either way.\n        Tali: ...I will make a map.\n        <<rep child 25>>\n    <<flag ch2_done>>\n    <<reward child_2>>\n<<else>>\n    Tali: Guard Brek. By the gate. Ask him, then come straight back and tell me!\n<<endif>>\n===\ntitle: brek_scene\n---\n<<if has("ch2_open") and not has("asked_brek")>>\n    You: Tali wants to know. Do orcs really eat children?\n    Brek: Tali wants... Ha! Tell her no. And tell her to stay away from my gate.\n    Brek: Between us? They are closer than the Chief says. The watch is doubled for a reason.\n    <<flag asked_brek>>\n<<endif>>\n===\n','title: healer_start\n---\n<<if has("ch2_done")>>\n    <<if has("told_truth")>>\n        Mira: He asks about his leg every day now. It is easier, being asked.\n    <<else>>\n        Mira: He still thinks it is only a sprain. He is laughing again. I do not know.\n    <<endif>>\n<<elseif has("ch2_open")>>\n    <<jump healer_ch2_back>>\n<<elseif has("ch1_done") and level() >= 14>>\n    <<jump healer_ch2>>\n<<elseif has("ch1_done")>>\n    Mira: Sit, if you must sit. Touch nothing with a label on it.\n<<elseif has("ch1_open")>>\n    <<jump healer_ch1_back>>\n<<else>>\n    <<jump healer_ch1>>\n<<endif>>\n===\ntitle: healer_ch1\n---\nMira: Hold still. This salve stings.\nYou: I am not hurt.\nMira: Then hold still anyway, you are in my light.\nMira: The wounds coming from the east go deep, and I am nearly out of riverbloom.\nMira: It grows wild in the Riverlands. So do things that eat people who pick it.\nYou: And you are telling me because...\nMira: Because you walked in here with no scars, and you are not afraid enough yet.\nMira: Three blooms. Whatever is out there tends to carry them off. Check its pockets.\n<<flag ch1_open>>\n===\ntitle: healer_ch1_back\n---\n<<if has_item("q_riverbloom", 3)>>\n    Mira: Three, and not crushed. Hm. You have careful hands. I did not expect that.\n    -> Ask who the salve is for.\n        You: Who is it for?\n        Mira: A scout named Ansa. Do not ask him how he is. He will say fine.\n        <<rep healer 15>>\n    -> Tell her the leg is not worth the blooms.\n        You: One leg is not worth three days of picking. Let him go.\n        Mira: Get out. Now.\n        <<rep healer -15>>\n    -> Ask what you are owed.\n        You: What is it worth?\n        Mira: To you, a coin purse. To him, a leg. Take your coins.\n        <<rep healer 5>>\n    <<take q_riverbloom 3>>\n    <<flag ch1_done>>\n    <<reward healer_1>>\n<<else>>\n    Mira: Three riverblooms, from the Riverlands. I cannot brew with good intentions.\n<<endif>>\n===\ntitle: healer_ch2\n---\nMira: Shut the door. Ansa\'s leg is not healing, and it is not going to.\nMira: He will walk with a stick for life. He will never scout again.\nMira: He has not asked. He thinks it is a sprain, and he is the happiest man here.\nYou: You have not told him.\nMira: I have told a hundred people worse. I find I cannot tell this one.\nMira: Go and sit with him. He sits outside my door, resting that leg. Then tell me.\n<<flag ch2_open>>\n===\ntitle: healer_ch2_back\n---\n<<if has("sat_ansa")>>\n    Mira: Well? You sat with him. What should I do?\n    -> "Tell him. He deserves the truth."\n        You: He keeps planning his next trip east. Tell him, before he tries the road.\n        Mira: Yes. I knew that. I only wanted somebody else to say it.\n        <<flag told_truth>>\n        <<rep healer 30>>\n    -> "Let him have the winter."\n        You: Let him laugh until the snow goes. The truth will still be here.\n        Mira: That is a kind thing to say. I am not sure it is a good one.\n        Mira: But I will take the winter, too.\n        <<rep healer 30>>\n    <<flag ch2_done>>\n    <<reward healer_2>>\n<<else>>\n    Mira: Sit with Ansa first. Outside my door, resting that leg. Then come and tell me.\n<<endif>>\n===\ntitle: ansa_scene\n---\n<<if has("ch2_open") and not has("sat_ansa")>>\n    Ansa: Sit, sit! You are the one Mira sends for flowers. Best salve in the world, this.\n    Ansa: Two more weeks and I am back out there. I know a shortcut past the mill.\n    Ansa: Do not tell Mira. She has a terrible worrying face.\n    You: How is the leg?\n    Ansa: Fine! Fine. Bit of a sprain.\n    <<flag sat_ansa>>\n<<endif>>\n===\n','title: hunter_start\n---\n<<if has("ch2_done")>>\n    Dahk: I keep the antler over my door. I tell people it is for luck.\n<<elseif has("ch2_open")>>\n    <<jump hunter_ch2_back>>\n<<elseif has("ch1_done") and level() >= 20>>\n    <<jump hunter_ch2>>\n<<elseif has("ch1_done")>>\n    Dahk: Tracks are still wrong. When the gate lets you past, come and find me.\n<<elseif has("ch1_open")>>\n    <<jump hunter_ch1_back>>\n<<elseif level() >= 8>>\n    <<jump hunter_ch1>>\n<<else>>\n    Dahk: The deer ran east. Strange for deer. Come back when you can handle a bow-shot of trouble.\n<<endif>>\n===\ntitle: hunter_ch1\n---\nDahk: The deer ran east. Strange for deer.\nYou: Is that strange? They are deer. They run places.\nDahk: Deer run from a thing, then circle home. These never circled.\nDahk: I lost the trail at the meadow\'s edge, where the ground gets hard.\nDahk: My eyes are not what they were. Yours are young. Go and read the ground for me.\n<<flag ch1_open>>\n===\ntitle: hunter_ch1_back\n---\n<<if has_item("q_bent_antler")>>\n    You: I found this at the trail\'s end. It had been snapped against a rock.\n    Dahk: They break those fighting, in autumn. It is spring. Nothing was fighting.\n    Dahk: A buck does that running flat out in the dark, not looking where it goes.\n    -> "What scares a whole herd that badly?"\n        Dahk: That is the right question. Nothing I have ever hunted.\n        <<rep hunter 15>>\n    -> "It was a deer. I would have shot it."\n        You: It was a deer. I would have put an arrow in it and eaten well.\n        Dahk: Then you and I have nothing more to say.\n        <<rep hunter -15>>\n    -> "Maybe just a bad night."\n        Dahk: Hm. Maybe. Thirty years, and I have never met a bad night that did that.\n        <<rep hunter 5>>\n    <<take q_bent_antler>>\n    <<flag ch1_done>>\n    <<reward hunter_1>>\n<<else>>\n    Dahk: The meadow\'s edge, where the ground gets hard. Read the trail. Bring me what you find.\n<<endif>>\n===\ntitle: hunter_ch2\n---\nDahk: They say you got through the East Gate. Then you can go where I cannot.\nDahk: Follow the trail past the Frontier. See where the herd finally stopped.\nDahk: I would go myself. I said that to my wife for eleven years, about something else.\nDahk: Do not take the bow-shot. Just look, then come home and tell me.\n<<flag ch2_open>>\n===\ntitle: hunter_ch2_back\n---\n<<if has("saw_herd")>>\n    You: I found them, past the south tower. They were standing still. All of them.\n    Dahk: Standing? Grazing?\n    You: Just standing, facing away from the east. They did not even look at me.\n    Dahk: ...Did you shoot?\n    -> "No. It did not feel right."\n        Dahk: Good. A hunter who cannot tell the difference is only a butcher.\n        <<rep hunter 30>>\n    -> "No. And I do not want to go back."\n        You: I have fought skeletons, and I would rather do that again.\n        Dahk: Then you learned the only thing I had to teach you.\n        <<rep hunter 30>>\n    <<flag ch2_done>>\n    <<reward hunter_2>>\n<<else>>\n    Dahk: Past the Frontier, past the south tower. Look, then come home.\n<<endif>>\n===\n','title: scout_start\n---\n<<if has("ch2_done")>>\n    <<if has("gave_ilun")>>\n        Ilun: I read it every night. I still do not sleep. But I read it.\n    <<else>>\n        Ilun: The Chief told me you brought it to him. I would have, too. Probably.\n    <<endif>>\n<<elseif has("ch2_open")>>\n    <<jump scout_ch2_back>>\n<<elseif has("ch1_done") and level() >= 28>>\n    <<jump scout_ch2>>\n<<elseif has("ch1_done")>>\n    Ilun: I told you all I am going to. Go and get strong. Then go and look.\n<<elseif level() >= 18>>\n    <<jump scout_ch1>>\n<<else>>\n    Ilun: I came back from the east. Do not ask.\n<<endif>>\n===\ntitle: scout_ch1\n---\nIlun: I came back from the east. Do not ask.\nYou: Two scouts did not come back. You went out with them.\nIlun: ...Who has been talking?\n-> Wait. Say nothing.\n    Ilun: You are good at that. Renn was good at that, too.\n    <<rep scout 15>>\n-> Press him. "What happened out there?"\n    Ilun: I said do not ask. Everyone asks. It comes out the same.\n    <<rep scout 5>>\nIlun: We split up at the burnt mill. Renn said wait for the light. I did not wait.\nIlun: I ran, and I kept running until I saw the gate. I left them there.\nYou: Why are you telling me this?\nIlun: Because you are going east, and you have that look. Do not stop at the mill.\n<<flag ch1_done>>\n<<reward scout_1>>\n===\ntitle: scout_ch2\n---\nIlun: You went past the mill. I can tell. Everybody comes back walking the same.\nIlun: Renn carried a satchel, with a letter for his sister in it. He wrote it every trip.\nIlun: If it is still there. I cannot go. I have tried. I get as far as the gate.\nYou: So you want me to go and look.\nIlun: I want a lot of things. That one is possible.\n<<flag ch2_open>>\n===\ntitle: scout_ch2_back\n---\n<<if has_item("q_torn_satchel")>>\n    You: It was under a beam at the mill. There is no sign of Renn. Or anyone.\n    Ilun: The letter. Is the letter in it?\n    You: It is. It is sealed. It is addressed to his sister, in the village.\n    -> Give the satchel to Ilun.\n        You: It should be you who decides this. You knew him.\n        Ilun: I do not deserve to hold it.\n        You: Nobody asked you that.\n        <<flag gave_ilun>>\n        <<rep scout 35>>\n    -> Tell him it goes to the Chief.\n        You: The Chief is still looking for them. He needs to see where this was found.\n        Ilun: Yes. That is right. That is what a good scout would do.\n        Ilun: Tell him I said so. Tell him... tell him I will talk to him. Soon.\n        <<rep scout 15>>\n    <<take q_torn_satchel>>\n    <<flag ch2_done>>\n    <<reward scout_2>>\n<<else>>\n    Ilun: The burnt mill, in the Scorched Edge. Under the fallen beams, if anywhere.\n<<endif>>\n===\n','title: pell_start\n---\n<<if has("ch2_done")>>\n    <<if has("read_letter")>>\n        Pell: She said yes! I mean, she said "ask me yourself, you coward." Same thing.\n    <<else>>\n        Pell: You never peeked? Not even once? You are the strangest person I have ever met.\n    <<endif>>\n<<elseif has("ch2_open")>>\n    <<jump pell_ch2_back>>\n<<elseif has("ch1_open")>>\n    <<jump pell_ch1_back>>\n<<elseif level() >= 18>>\n    <<jump pell_ch1>>\n<<else>>\n    Pell: Courier Pell, fastest legs in the village! Come back when the gate will let you through.\n<<endif>>\n===\ntitle: pell_ch1\n---\nPell: You! You are going to the Frontier. Everyone with a sword goes to the Frontier.\nPell: I am the courier. I take letters. I am extremely good at it, and I have a bad knee.\nYou: You ran over here. I watched you run.\nPell: A very sudden knee. Please. This one goes to Guard Dal, at the east wall.\nPell: Do not read it. It is private. It is about... grain.\n<<give q_sealed_letter>>\n<<flag ch1_open>>\n===\ntitle: pell_ch1_back\n---\n<<if has_item("q_folded_reply")>>\n    Pell: You got a reply? Give it! Is it long? Long is good. Is it short? Is it short?\n    <<take q_folded_reply>>\n    Pell: "Stop writing about grain, Pell." Oh, thank goodness. She read it!\n    You: The letter was for Guard Dal.\n    Pell: Dal\'s sister works the stores at the gate. Dal reads her the letters. She cannot read yet.\n    You: So Dal reads your love letters out loud, to his own sister.\n    Pell: ...When you put it like that, it sounds worse than grain.\n    <<rep pell 20>>\n    <<flag ch1_done>>\n    <<flag ch2_open>>\n    <<reward pell_1>>\n    Pell: One more. A real one this time. I wrote it myself. Twice. Take it to Dal.\n    <<give q_sealed_letter>>\n<<else>>\n    Pell: Guard Dal, at the east wall of the Frontier. And mind the letter. It is about grain.\n<<endif>>\n===\ntitle: pell_ch2_back\n---\n<<if has_item("q_folded_reply")>>\n    Pell: Well? What did she say? No, wait. Do not tell me. Did you read it? Did you?\n    <<take q_folded_reply>>\n    <<if has("read_letter")>>\n        You: I read it. And so did Dal, out loud, and the whole watch heard.\n        Pell: The whole...? Oh no. And what did they say?\n        You: Guard Ven cried. She says ask her yourself, you coward.\n    <<else>>\n        You: I did not read it. It is yours.\n        Pell: You carried my whole heart across the Frontier, and you did not peek?\n    <<endif>>\n    Pell: I am going to ask her. On my knee. The bad one. It will look more sincere.\n    <<rep pell 30>>\n    <<flag ch2_done>>\n    <<reward pell_2>>\n<<elseif has_item("q_sealed_letter")>>\n    Pell: Guard Dal. East wall. Quick as you like, and no peeking. Well. Your choice.\n<<else>>\n    Pell: Dal should have a reply by now. Go and ask him for it, would you?\n<<endif>>\n===\ntitle: dal_scene\n---\n<<if has_item("q_sealed_letter") and not has("first_reply")>>\n    Dal: Another one from Pell? Grain, I expect. Hand it here.\n    <<take q_sealed_letter>>\n    Dal: "My dearest grain." Honestly. Here is her answer. Do not lose it.\n    <<give q_folded_reply>>\n    <<flag first_reply>>\n<<elseif has_item("q_sealed_letter")>>\n    Dal: This one is thick. Will you be reading it first? Everyone else has.\n    -> Read it with him.\n        You: Go on, then. Read it out.\n        Dal: Hey, Ven! Tor! Come and hear this one! He has written a poem!\n        <<flag read_letter>>\n        Pell: You read it. With the whole watch. I heard them laughing from here.\n        <<rep pell -12>>\n    -> Hand it over sealed.\n        You: It is not mine to read.\n        Dal: Huh. Nobody ever says that.\n        Dal: Fine. Tell the courier his letter has better manners than he does.\n        <<rep guard_dal -12>>\n    <<take q_sealed_letter>>\n    Dal: I will read it to her tonight. Here. She wrote this for him last week, just in case.\n    <<give q_folded_reply>>\n<<endif>>\n===\n','title: wren_start\n---\n<<if has("ch2_done")>>\n    <<if has("kept_ferry")>>\n        Wren: Bell still rings at dusk. Nobody comes. I still ring it. I am well, you know.\n    <<else>>\n        Wren: I sold the boat to a fisher. I am walking north. Mind the bank, it is soft there.\n    <<endif>>\n<<elseif has("ch2_open")>>\n    <<jump wren_ch2_back>>\n<<elseif has("ch1_done") and world("questDone:flowerBoss")>>\n    <<jump wren_ch2>>\n<<elseif has("ch1_done")>>\n    Wren: Bridge is shut while that flower sits on it. When it is gone, come and see me.\n<<elseif has("ch1_open")>>\n    <<jump wren_ch1_back>>\n<<else>>\n    <<jump wren_ch1>>\n<<endif>>\n===\ntitle: wren_ch1\n---\nWren: Ferry is closed. Ferry has been closed since spring. Do not ask me about the bridge.\nYou: I was going to ask about the bell. There is a rope here, and no bell on it.\nWren: You have good eyes, and bad manners.\nWren: My brother Teo rang that bell. Rang it every dusk, so boats could find the landing.\nWren: One night the bell got taken. Teo went up the bank to get it back.\nWren: Something up there likes shiny things. Likes them enough to keep them.\nWren: I do not ask for much. I am asking for a bell. Teo can make his own way home.\n<<flag ch1_open>>\n===\ntitle: wren_ch1_back\n---\n<<if has_item("q_ferry_bell")>>\n    You: It was on one of those things up the bank. Just the bell. I looked. Nothing else.\n    Wren: No. There would not be.\n    Wren: Dent in it. He dropped it off the landing, the first week. Got a real telling off.\n    -> Say you are sorry.\n        You: I am sorry about your brother.\n        Wren: Everyone is. It does not row the boat.\n        <<rep wren 10>>\n    -> Offer to hang it up for her.\n        You: Here. Hold the rope. I will tie it on.\n        Wren: ...You tie a terrible knot. Give it here. Yes. Like that.\n        <<rep wren 20>>\n    <<take q_ferry_bell>>\n    <<flag ch1_done>>\n    <<reward wren_1>>\n<<else>>\n    Wren: Up the bank, where the bad things live. Small brass bell, with a dent in it.\n<<endif>>\n===\ntitle: wren_ch2\n---\nWren: So you killed the flower. Bridge is open. Nobody needs a ferry now, then.\nYou: You could still run it.\nWren: For who? I have been ringing a bell for a boat that does not come. Who for, I ask you.\nWren: There is a mooring post at the old south landing. He carved our names on it, as kids.\nWren: I want to know if it is still standing. I find I cannot go and look.\n<<flag ch2_open>>\n===\ntitle: wren_ch2_back\n---\n<<if has("saw_post")>>\n    You: It is still standing. Both names. Someone has cut a new mark under them.\n    Wren: A new one? What kind of a mark?\n    You: A little boat. It looks recent. It could be anybody.\n    Wren: ...Could be anybody. Yes.\n    -> "You should stay, and keep ringing that bell."\n        You: If someone is out there, they will be looking for that bell at dusk.\n        Wren: That is a cruel thing to say to me. Kind, and cruel.\n        Wren: Fine. One more year. Then we will see.\n        <<flag kept_ferry>>\n        <<rep wren 30>>\n    -> "You should go. You have waited long enough."\n        You: You have done more than anyone could ask. Go and find out what else there is.\n        Wren: Forty years on this water. I do not know what else there is.\n        Wren: ...I suppose that is rather the point.\n        <<rep wren 30>>\n    <<flag ch2_done>>\n    <<reward wren_2>>\n<<else>>\n    Wren: The old south landing. The post with the names on it. Is it standing or not.\n<<endif>>\n===\n','title: kessa_start\n---\n<<if has("ch2_done")>>\n    <<if has("spared_tor")>>\n        Kessa: Tor is on double watch for a year. He thanks me for it. It is very annoying.\n    <<else>>\n        Kessa: The new man on the south wall is hopeless. The rations add up, though.\n    <<endif>>\n<<elseif has("ch2_open")>>\n    <<jump kessa_ch2_back>>\n<<elseif has("ch1_done") and level() >= 24>>\n    <<jump kessa_ch2>>\n<<elseif has("ch1_done")>>\n    Kessa: Still counting, still short. Go on and fight something. I will find you when I need you.\n<<elseif has("ch1_open")>>\n    <<jump kessa_ch1_back>>\n<<else>>\n    <<jump kessa_ch1>>\n<<endif>>\n===\ntitle: kessa_ch1\n---\nKessa: Warden Kessa. I run this wall. You are in the way of it.\nYou: I only came to help.\nKessa: Then count. We are short on rations, every week, and it is not the rats.\nKessa: Rats do not sign the ledger. And rats do not eat only the cured meat.\nKessa: Something has been dragging sacks out past the east yard. Find me one.\n<<flag ch1_open>>\n===\ntitle: kessa_ch1_back\n---\n<<if has_item("q_gnawed_sack")>>\n    You: Found this in the long grass. Empty, and not chewed. Those are knife cuts.\n    Kessa: So somebody wants it to look like animals. Somebody here.\n    -> Offer to ask around, quietly.\n        You: I am new here. People talk in front of me. Let me ask around.\n        Kessa: Hm. You have a sneak\'s instincts. I mean that as a compliment. Mostly.\n        <<rep kessa 15>>\n    -> Tell her the whole wall is rotten.\n        You: Maybe the watch is rotten. Starting with the ones doing the counting.\n        Kessa: Say that where the watch can hear it. See how your count goes.\n        <<rep kessa -12>>\n    -> Tell her to line them up and search them.\n        You: Search the barracks. Tonight. Catch them with it.\n        Kessa: And have the whole wall hate me by morning? Spoken like someone just passing through.\n        <<rep kessa 5>>\n    <<take q_gnawed_sack>>\n    <<flag ch1_done>>\n    <<reward kessa_1>>\n<<else>>\n    Kessa: Past the east yard, in the long grass. An empty ration sack. Bring it to me.\n<<endif>>\n===\ntitle: kessa_ch2\n---\nKessa: Take my ledger. Ask Tor, Dal, Ven. Someone\'s watch lines up with every missing sack.\nKessa: I have my suspicion. I want yours, and I do not want it to match by accident.\n<<give q_ration_ledger>>\n<<flag ch2_open>>\n===\ntitle: kessa_ch2_back\n---\n<<if has("found_tor")>>\n    You: It is Tor. He has been taking the meat out to the south tower. There is a family.\n    You: Burnt out of the east, hiding by the wall. Two kids. They are starving.\n    Kessa: ...I see. And the ledger?\n    Kessa: If I let this go, every guard here learns he may steal for a good reason.\n    Kessa: You found him. So I am asking you. What would you do?\n    -> "Keep him. Bring the family in, and feed them properly."\n        You: Punish him if you have to. But bring them inside the wall.\n        Kessa: Double watch for a year. And now I have two more mouths on my ledger.\n        Kessa: Fine. That is the last soft thing I ever do. Do not tell anyone.\n        <<flag spared_tor>>\n        <<rep kessa 30>>\n    -> "Send him away. The wall has to hold."\n        You: The wall only works if the rules do. Send him off. Feed them from your own table.\n        Kessa: Hard, and fair. You will be good at this. I am sorry for that.\n        <<rep kessa 30>>\n    <<take q_ration_ledger>>\n    <<flag ch2_done>>\n    <<reward kessa_2>>\n<<elseif has_item("q_ration_ledger")>>\n    Kessa: Ledger in hand, talk to Tor, Dal and Ven. Then come and tell me who.\n<<else>>\n    Kessa: You had my ledger. Come back when you have got an answer as well.\n<<endif>>\n===\ntitle: tor_scene\n---\n<<if has_item("q_ration_ledger") and not has("found_tor")>>\n    Tor: Warden\'s ledger, is it? Stay on the road. The wall has gaps past the bend.\n    You: Every sack went missing on your watch, Tor.\n    Tor: ...Did it.\n    -> Say nothing, and wait.\n        Tor: Fine. South tower, at dusk. Come and see. Then tell her what you like.\n        <<rep kessa 5>>\n    -> Tell him you will find out either way.\n        Tor: Yes, I expect you will. South tower. See it yourself, before you judge me.\n    You: Two kids and their mother were by the tower, wrapped in a watch cloak.\n    <<flag found_tor>>\n<<endif>>\n===\n','title: oda_start\n---\n<<if has("ch2_done")>>\n    <<if has("kept_playing")>>\n        Oda: Listen. Same little song. Terrible little song. Lovely, is it not?\n    <<else>>\n        Oda: Quiet out here now. I sweep that spot by the door anyway. Force of habit, dear.\n    <<endif>>\n<<elseif has("ch2_open")>>\n    <<jump oda_ch2_back>>\n<<elseif has("ch1_done") and level() >= 34>>\n    <<jump oda_ch2>>\n<<elseif has("ch1_done")>>\n    Oda: Go on, dear. I have ashes to sort. They will not sort themselves.\n<<elseif has("ch1_open")>>\n    <<jump oda_ch1_back>>\n<<else>>\n    <<jump oda_ch1>>\n<<endif>>\n===\ntitle: oda_ch1\n---\nOda: Mind your boots, dear. That was somebody\'s kitchen.\nYou: There is nothing left here. What are you looking for?\nOda: Nothing in particular. Spoons. Hinges. You would be surprised what a fire leaves.\nOda: I have sorted this whole town by now. Everything in its street, where it was.\nYou: Why?\nOda: Somebody ought to know where everything was.\nOda: There is one thing I never found. A little music box. Those brutes took everything shiny.\n<<flag ch1_open>>\n===\ntitle: oda_ch1_back\n---\n<<if has_item("q_music_box")>>\n    You: One of them was carrying this. It is burnt, but I think it still works.\n    Oda: Oh. Oh, you silly thing. Give it here. Careful of the lid.\n    Narrator: She turns the little key. Nothing. Then four thin notes, and a long, long wait.\n    Oda: It plays worse than ever. My daughter never could leave it alone.\n    -> Ask about her daughter.\n        You: Where is she now?\n        Oda: Moved west, years ago, before all this. Writes when she remembers. Ha! Do not fret.\n        <<rep oda 20>>\n    -> Tell her the town is better gone.\n        You: The town burned. Let it. You are sorting a grave.\n        Oda: ...Yes. Well. Off you go, dear. Mind the ash.\n        <<rep oda -12>>\n    -> Say nothing, and listen.\n        Oda: You are a good listener, dear. Nobody is, out here. The ash does not chat.\n        <<rep oda 15>>\n    <<take q_music_box>>\n    <<flag ch1_done>>\n    <<reward oda_1>>\n<<else>>\n    Oda: A little music box. Those brutes out in the ash are carrying it, I shouldn\'t wonder.\n<<endif>>\n===\ntitle: oda_ch2\n---\nOda: My daughter wrote. She wants me to come west, and stop being a daft old woman.\nOda: There is a sign at the end of the ash road. Our town\'s name. I painted it, you know.\nOda: If it is still up, I shall stay. If it is gone, then I shall go. Fair is fair.\nOda: You go and look. I do not trust myself to read it honestly.\n<<flag ch2_open>>\n===\ntitle: oda_ch2_back\n---\n<<if has("saw_sign")>>\n    You: It is gone. Burnt to the post. Just the post, and a nail in it.\n    Oda: Well, there we are, then. Fair is fair.\n    Oda: ...A nail, you say.\n    You: One nail.\n    -> "A nail is not a sign. Go west."\n        You: You made a deal. She is waiting for you. Go and see your daughter.\n        Oda: Bossy. Good. Somebody ought to be. I will pack the spoons.\n        <<rep oda 30>>\n    -> "You could always paint a new one."\n        You: You painted the last one. You still have your hands. What does a sign cost?\n        Oda: You are a terrible influence, dear. Oh, I do hope I have some red left.\n        <<flag kept_playing>>\n        <<rep oda 30>>\n    <<flag ch2_done>>\n    <<reward oda_2>>\n<<else>>\n    Oda: The sign at the end of the ash road. Is it up, or is it not? Off you pop, dear.\n<<endif>>\n===\n','title: hale_start\n---\n<<if has("ch2_done")>>\n    <<if story_flag("grot", "freed")>>\n        Hale: Tags came in. Someone let a prisoner go on my watch. I have decided not to know who.\n    <<else>>\n        Hale: Tags are in, and the widows get paid. That is more than the generals ever did.\n    <<endif>>\n<<elseif has("ch2_open")>>\n    <<jump hale_ch2_back>>\n<<elseif has("ch1_done") and level() >= 46>>\n    <<jump hale_ch2>>\n<<elseif has("ch1_done")>>\n    Hale: Eat something. You look like I feel. I will have work for you soon enough.\n<<elseif has("ch1_open")>>\n    <<jump hale_ch1_back>>\n<<else>>\n    <<jump hale_ch1>>\n<<endif>>\n===\ntitle: hale_ch1\n---\nHale: Quartermaster Hale. If you are here for the glory, it is further on. I do boots.\nYou: You are camped in the middle of orc country.\nHale: Somebody has to be. The army moved east. The boots stayed, and so did I.\nHale: We lost men out here. Each of them wore a tag. Bring in a tag, and a widow gets paid.\nHale: No tag, no silver. Whoever wrote that rule never stood out here. Orcs keep them.\nHale: Five tags. I have asked everyone else. They are all more important than boots.\n<<flag ch1_open>>\n===\ntitle: hale_ch1_back\n---\n<<if has_item("q_supply_tag", 5)>>\n    Hale: Five. Let me see. Harrow. Bel. Oh, Bel. I knew him. Terrible cook. Hm.\n    -> Ask how many are still out there.\n        You: How many tags are still missing?\n        Hale: Do not ask a quartermaster that unless you want the real number. Hundreds.\n        <<rep hale 15>>\n    -> Ask for your pay.\n        You: So do I get paid, too?\n        Hale: Ha! Yes. I like you. No one else here has mentioned money in weeks.\n        <<rep hale 10>>\n    <<take q_supply_tag 5>>\n    <<flag ch1_done>>\n    <<reward hale_1>>\n<<else>>\n    Hale: Five tags. The orcs out in the Wastes wear them. Like trophies. Go and get them back.\n<<endif>>\n===\ntitle: hale_ch2\n---\nHale: We caught a young one. Orc, half my height, hiding by the south wagons, eating my oats.\nHale: The Warcamp pays for prisoners who can talk. My orders are to march him there.\nHale: You are heading that way, so he is your problem. Grot, or that is the noise he makes.\nHale: Go and see him. Then tell me whether he walks to the Warcamp.\n<<flag ch2_open>>\n===\ntitle: hale_ch2_back\n---\n<<if story_flag("grot", "freed")>>\n    You: He got away, in the night. Must have been the ropes.\n    Hale: Good rope, that. Very good rope. I tied it myself.\n    Hale: ...I will mark it as lost. Do not look at me like that. Get out of my tent.\n    <<flag ch2_done>>\n    <<reward hale_2>>\n<<elseif story_flag("grot", "handed_over")>>\n    You: Grot is on his way to the Warcamp, under guard.\n    Hale: Good. Orders are orders. Did he cry?\n    You: No. He asked me if it was far.\n    Hale: ...Yes. They do that. Thank you. Now leave me to my boots.\n    <<rep hale 35>>\n    <<flag ch2_done>>\n    <<reward hale_2>>\n<<else>>\n    Hale: The little one, by the south wagons. Go and see him, then tell me what you decide.\n<<endif>>\n===\n','title: grot_start\n---\n<<if has("freed")>>\n    Grot: Not your camp. Your camp has ropes. I am only here for the oats. Sshh.\n<<elseif has("handed_over")>>\n    Narrator: The rope lies coiled by the wagons. Someone has left half a bag of oats beside it.\n<<elseif has("ch1_open")>>\n    <<jump grot_ch1_back>>\n<<elseif story_flag("hale", "ch2_open")>>\n    <<jump grot_ch1>>\n<<else>>\n    Narrator: Something small rustles under the wagons, and goes very still.\n<<endif>>\n===\ntitle: grot_ch1\n---\nGrot: You are big. Do big ones eat oats? The rope man eats oats. The rope man is sad.\nYou: You speak our words.\nGrot: Some. Trader taught me. Trader said orcs are all stupid. Trader was not very smart.\nYou: Why were you all the way out here?\nGrot: Everyone at home goes. Big ones go, and go, and do not say why. I went the other way.\nGrot: I had a charm from my nan. Lost it in the rocks, running. I want it. Then rope, okay.\n<<flag ch1_open>>\n===\ntitle: grot_ch1_back\n---\n<<if has_item("q_orc_charm")>>\n    You: Is this it? Bone, with a bit of red string?\n    Grot: Nan! ...Yes. Thank you, big one. You may eat one oat.\n    Grot: So. Rope man says I go to the Warcamp. Is it far?\n    -> Cut the rope. "It is that way. Do not stop running."\n        You: Go. West is safer. Keep away from the roads.\n        Grot: You will get in trouble. Rope man will be sad.\n        You: The rope man is always sad.\n        Grot: ...Yes. Bye, big one. Eat more oats.\n        <<flag freed>>\n        <<rep grot 40>>\n        <<reward grot_1>>\n    -> Keep the rope on. "I am sorry. I have to take you in."\n        You: I am sorry. It is not far. I will make sure they feed you.\n        Grot: Okay. You came back with Nan. So I know you are not lying.\n        <<flag handed_over>>\n        <<reward grot_1>>\n    <<take q_orc_charm>>\n    <<rep grot 15>>\n    <<flag ch1_done>>\n<<else>>\n    Grot: In the rocks. Past the big bone pile. Bone charm, with red string. Please, big one.\n<<endif>>\n===\n','title: marl_start\n---\n<<if has("ch2_done")>>\n    Marl: Sohn kept his word, then? Good. That old goat owes me for thirty years of salt.\n<<elseif has("ch2_open")>>\n    Marl: Mind that parcel. Elder Sohn, by the village fire. Through the cave, over the river.\n<<elseif has("ch1_done") and world("questDone:slimeBoss")>>\n    <<jump marl_ch2>>\n<<elseif has("ch1_done")>>\n    Marl: Wheel is sound. Road is not. That big slime still sits at the cave mouth.\n<<elseif has("ch1_open")>>\n    <<jump marl_ch1_back>>\n<<else>>\n    <<jump marl_ch1>>\n<<endif>>\n===\ntitle: marl_ch1\n---\nMarl: Ho! A person! A real one, walking upright. I had begun to talk to the mule.\nMarl: There is no mule. There was. That is rather the trouble.\nYou: Where am I? I woke on the shore. I do not remember much else.\nMarl: Simula. Sim\'la, if you ask the old folk. The first place, they say.\nMarl: Then you are ahead of me. I remember all of it, and I would give a lot not to.\nMarl: Slimes got into my cart. Ate the axle grease, and the mule ran off at the smell.\nMarl: Slime jelly makes fair grease, mind. Three good lumps, and this wheel turns again.\n<<flag ch1_open>>\n===\ntitle: marl_ch1_back\n---\n<<if has_item("q_slime_jelly", 3)>>\n    You: Three lumps. It moved the whole way here. I would rather not discuss it.\n    Marl: Nobody ever does. Hand it over.\n    Marl: Ha! Listen to that. Not a squeak. You have a good pair of hands, stranger.\n    -> Ask what is past the meadow.\n        You: What is out there, past the grass?\n        Marl: A cave, a river, then a village with a fire that stays lit. Head for the fire.\n        <<rep marl 10>>\n    -> Ask about the mule.\n        You: Do you want me to keep an eye out for the mule?\n        Marl: ...Her name is Dot. Nobody has asked me that. Thank you. Yes. Keep an eye out.\n        <<rep marl 15>>\n    <<take q_slime_jelly 3>>\n    <<flag ch1_done>>\n    <<reward marl_1>>\n<<else>>\n    Marl: Three lumps of slime jelly. The fights around here will get you plenty.\n<<endif>>\n===\ntitle: marl_ch2\n---\nMarl: You beat that great slime? Then the road is open, and I am too old to walk it.\nMarl: Take this to Elder Sohn, in the village. Through the cave, then over the river.\nYou: What is in it?\nMarl: Salt, and an apology. The salt is the heavy part.\n<<give q_marl_parcel>>\n<<flag ch2_open>>\n===\ntitle: sohn_scene\n---\n<<if has("ch2_done")>>\n    Sohn: Salt, after thirty years. Marl always did think slowly. Sit by the fire a while.\n<<elseif has_item("q_marl_parcel")>>\n    You: From Marl, the carter. He is stuck out in the meadow, talking to nobody.\n    Sohn: Marl. Is he still alive? The old fool. What has he sent me?\n    Sohn: Salt. And a letter. Hm. He says he is sorry about the boat. We sank it together.\n    -> "You should send word back."\n        You: He would like to hear from you. He would never say so.\n        Sohn: No. He would not. I will send a boy out with a cart and a fresh mule.\n        <<rep marl 30>>\n    -> "He said the salt was the heavy part."\n        You: He said the salt was the heavy part.\n        Sohn: Ha! He would. He never could say a thing straight. Thank you for the walk.\n        <<rep marl 25>>\n    <<take q_marl_parcel>>\n    <<flag ch2_done>>\n    <<reward marl_2>>\n<<else>>\n    Sohn: I remember when the east was only forest.\n<<endif>>\n===\n','title: sunna_start\n---\n<<if has("ch2_done")>>\n    Sunna: It is only a cave now. Bad air, worse company. I like it better.\n<<elseif has("ch2_open")>>\n    <<jump sunna_ch2_back>>\n<<elseif has("ch1_done") and world("questDone:knightBoss")>>\n    <<jump sunna_ch2>>\n<<elseif has("ch1_done")>>\n    Sunna: That knight still walks the far end. I can hear him from here. Every night.\n<<elseif has("ch1_open")>>\n    <<jump sunna_ch1_back>>\n<<else>>\n    <<jump sunna_ch1>>\n<<endif>>\n===\ntitle: sunna_ch1\n---\nSunna: Stop there. Do not step left. Or do, but I will not be coming to fetch you.\nYou: What is left?\nSunna: A long way down. I lost my lamp on the way up from it. Now I sit here, in the dark.\nYou: You are a miner?\nSunna: Was. Forty days ago there was ore in this hill, and the dead stayed where we put them.\nSunna: My lamp is by the old cart rails, past the first bones. Brass. It still has oil.\n<<flag ch1_open>>\n===\ntitle: sunna_ch1_back\n---\n<<if has_item("q_miner_lamp")>>\n    You: Brass, you said. It still has oil.\n    Sunna: Give it here. Oh, that is better. You have no idea how much better that is.\n    Sunna: Now look at you. You are bleeding, and you did not even notice, did you.\n    -> Ask what woke the dead.\n        You: What woke them? The skeletons?\n        Sunna: I dig. I do not ask. If you find out, do not come and tell me.\n        <<rep sunna 10>>\n    -> Ask her to come out with you.\n        You: Come out with me. The way back is clear enough for now.\n        Sunna: Not yet. There is a man at the far end, in armor. I need to know he has stopped.\n        <<rep sunna 15>>\n    <<take q_miner_lamp>>\n    <<flag ch1_done>>\n    <<reward sunna_1>>\n<<else>>\n    Sunna: By the old cart rails, past the first bones. Brass lamp. Mind the left.\n<<endif>>\n===\ntitle: sunna_ch2\n---\nSunna: It has gone quiet. The far end has gone quiet. That was you?\nYou: The Bone Knight is down.\nSunna: Grandfather told of a guard who would never leave his post. I thought it was a story.\nSunna: He said they each wore a tin star. The bones here still carry such things.\nSunna: I would like to have one, to bury. It seems the least anyone could do.\n<<flag ch2_open>>\n===\ntitle: sunna_ch2_back\n---\n<<if has_item("q_old_badge")>>\n    You: Tin, with a star. It came off one of them, down here.\n    Sunna: That is the one. Or one just like it. I find I do not mind which.\n    -> Help her bury it.\n        You: I will dig, if you hold the lamp.\n        Sunna: You dig like a farmer. ...It will do. Rest now, whoever you were.\n        <<rep sunna 30>>\n    -> Tell her to keep it.\n        You: Keep it. Someone should remember him.\n        Sunna: Hm. Yes. I know a village over the river. They could use someone who remembers.\n        <<rep sunna 25>>\n    <<take q_old_badge>>\n    <<flag ch2_done>>\n    <<reward sunna_2>>\n<<else>>\n    Sunna: A little tin star. The bones in this cave might still carry one. Have a look.\n<<endif>>\n===\n','title: wyn_start\n---\n<<if world("prof:unlocked")>>\n    <<if not world("prof:rod_given")>>\n        Wyn: One more thing. Here. A rod.\n        Wyn: The river is full of fish. Go catch us dinner.\n        <<give_item tool_bronze_rod>>\n        <<world_flag prof:rod_given>>\n    <<else>>\n        Wyn: Still got that tent? Good. Best thing I ever lost.\n        Wyn: Plant, water, gather. Then take it all to the huts.\n    <<endif>>\n<<elseif has("ch1_open")>>\n    <<jump wyn_ch1_back>>\n<<else>>\n    <<jump wyn_ch1>>\n<<endif>>\n===\ntitle: wyn_ch1\n---\nWyn: You there. Do you like roofs?\nYou: I have never really had one.\nWyn: Then help me get mine back. Slimes chased me off my old camp.\nWyn: My bundle is still out in the west meadow. Off the road, in the quiet.\nWyn: Bring it here. I have a tent for you. A small one. A start.\n<<flag ch1_open>>\n===\ntitle: wyn_ch1_back\n---\n<<if has_item("q_wyn_bundle")>>\n    Wyn: That is it! Look at it. Still smells of rain.\n    <<take q_wyn_bundle>>\n    Wyn: Here. A satchel, a tent, an axe, a pick, a can and a rod. All yours.\n    <<if not world("prof:unlocked")>>\n        <<give_item bag_satchel>>\n        <<give_item key_tent>>\n        <<give_item tool_bronze_axe>>\n        <<give_item tool_bronze_pickaxe>>\n        <<give_item tool_watering_can>>\n        <<give_item tool_bronze_rod>>\n        <<give_item seed_oak 2>>\n        <<give_item seed_copper 2>>\n        <<give_item seed_sunleaf 2>>\n        <<world_flag prof:unlocked>>\n        <<world_flag prof:rod_given>>\n    <<endif>>\n    Wyn: Pitch it somewhere quiet. Plant a seed. Come back and show me.\n    <<rep homesteader 20>>\n    <<flag ch1_done>>\n    <<reward wyn_1>>\n<<else>>\n    Wyn: West meadow, off the road. The bundle is red. Slimes love red.\n<<endif>>\n===\n'],t.l)
